<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP oil production up, gas output down.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP oil production up, gas output down.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Monday its oil and condensate production for December increased to 5.4 million barrels, up 3.0 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The rise was due mainly to higher European output, in particular from the Liverpool Bay field, which was partially offset by a lower contribution from the Americas as a result of divestments, the company said in its monthly production report.</p>
<p>BHP said Australian and Asian production was relatively stable with increased output from the Wanaea/Cossack field on the North West Shelf a highlight.  </p>
<p>Gas production eased compared with the same month last year primarily as a result of property sales in the Americas.</p>
<p>&quot;Bass Strait gas production has declined, while Europe gas production increased as a result of Liverpool Bay gas production and a higher contribution from the Bruce gas field in the North Sea,&quot; BHP said.  </p>
